# Tiny Pascal / P-Machine

P-Machine in ROM (unified build). Python cross-compiler: `pascal_compiler.py`. Language ref: `pascal/LANGUAGE.md`.

## Compile & run (cross-compiler)

```bash
source .venv/bin/activate
python pascal_compiler.py pascal/examples/hello.pas -o roms/apps/current/pascal/hello.bin
python simulate.py --autorun --program roms/apps/current/pascal/hello.bin --max-cycles 1000000 --quiet
```

Binaries load at **0x8400** with native stub → `JSR PM_ENTRY`. Kernel `p` command runs raw P-code at 0x8400.

For older kernel EEPROMs: `./scripts/build-apps.sh --abi v1.2.101 --pascal` (uses `PM_ENTRY` from `kernel/abi/v1.2.101/symbols.asm`).

## P-Machine RAM

- State: 0xB000–0xB00B
- Eval stack: 0xB100–0xB1FF (16-bit values, grows up)
- Variable frame: 0xB200–0xB3FF
- Call stack: 0xBA00–0xBAFF

## On-board IDE (not in ROM)

Build: `apps/tinypascal_ide.asm` → `roms/apps/current/asm/tinypascal_ide.bin`

- Upload: **`u020000`**; run: **`r020000`**
- Editor source: expansion RAM 0x010000+; compiler workspace ~0x016000 (`pascal/consts.asm`)
- **`lo` paste**: lines **≤ 79 characters** (80 chars + null breaks loader)
- Editor: `n` new, `lo` load, `r` run, `q` quit

## Regression

After changes to `pascal/compiler.asm`, `pmachine.asm`, `editor.asm`, or Python compiler:

```bash
./generate-all.sh
python pascal/tools/run_tinypascal_suite.py
python pascal/tools/run_tinypascal_suite.py --cross
```

**Known limitation**: on-board compiler miscompiles some `string` variable assignments; suite uses string literals only.

Full P-code opcodes and syntax: `AGENTS.md`.
